From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: the Status column shows a glyph for each cloud state; cldapi traces name files

File Explorer shows a cloud file's Status with a small picture beside the words. The Status column now does too, with our own drawings: an outlined cloud when the file is online only, a check in an outlined circle when it is on this device, a check in a filled circle when it is always kept here, and two arrows when its sync is pending. cldapi's traces now name the file of each placeholder call and the flags of each placeholder created, to see which states a sync client sets.
---
diff --git a/dlls/cldapi/main.c b/dlls/cldapi/main.c
index 6ef346d..8fb2148 100644
--- a/dlls/cldapi/main.c
+++ b/dlls/cldapi/main.c
@@ -280,6 +280,16 @@ static BOOL handle_path(HANDLE handle, WCHAR *path, DWORD len)
     return TRUE;
 }
 
+/* Stained Glass OS 6256: the file a handle names, for traces */
+static const char *debugstr_handle(HANDLE handle)
+{
+    WCHAR path[MAX_PATH];
+
+    if (!TRACE_ON(cldapi)) return "";
+    if (!handle_path(handle, path, MAX_PATH)) return wine_dbg_sprintf("%p", handle);
+    return wine_dbg_sprintf("%p %s", handle, debugstr_w(path));
+}
